  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Les Rôtisseurs de la Côte is at 500 rue du Port, in Cavalaire-sur-Mer, on the harbour. The restaurant's website lists specialities of bull meat, beef and spit-roasted meats, and its Facebook page mentions meats and fish seared over a wood fire, a menu of tapas to share and DJ evenings every weekend. The Gulf of Saint-Tropez tourist office lists it as a traditional restaurant and pizzeria, with home-made dishes and wifi.</p>

      <h2>Good to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The restaurant's website offers phone bookings on 04 94 15 46 47 and welcomes groups of 20 to 25 people. Published opening hours vary by source: the website announces lunch and dinner except Sunday, with Sunday evening in July and evenings only every day in July and August; the Facebook page says "Monday to Saturday" and "every evening"; the tourist office says open every day all year. Call before you come, especially for lunch.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: no official source consulted mentions dogs; ask on the phone whether your dog can sit with you on the terrace before booking.</div>    </div>

